In the meantime, I thought you might like to hear how this went somewhere
similar. A Director of Composition at a mid-sized public college we work
with told us after their first term:

  "We were braced for students to game it. Instead they revised more.
   Our tutors stopped spending the first ten minutes of every session on
   thesis statements and started talking about argument."

And if it's useful for the wider team, we're running a free webinar,
"Feedback that students actually read: rubric-aligned AI in first-year
writing," on Thursday 18 March at 10:00 Pacific. Happy to save seats for
anyone at Saltmarren or across the Tarrow system - just say the word.

Thanks again for all your time, Mara. Delphine, great to see you on the
thread as always!

Best,
